WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.720
A rolling stone gathers no moss.

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.320
But a walking, talking pile of them?

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.560
That's another story.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.540
Marvel fans noticed a slight change to Korg
between his appearances in Thor: Ragnarok

00:00:10.549 --> 00:00:15.349
and Avengers: Endgame, which illustrates the
extent to which he, Miek, and Thor let themselves

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:17.420
go during Endgame's five-year time jump.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.790
When Bruce Banner and Rocket arrive in New
Asgard to attempt to recruit the Thunder God

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:27.080
for the Avengers' time heist, Korg's lovely
blue hue is also marked by patches of green.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.680
Yes, the affable rock dude is suffering from
a bit of a moss infestation.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.360
"Long time, no see."

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.420
"Beer's in the bucket!

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.940
Feel free to log on to the Wi-fi!"

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.420
If you pause the movie to examine him closely,
which you can now that Avengers: Endgame is

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.880
available digitally, you can see that he's
downright lousy with the stuff.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.800
Astute Reddit user AmazingSpdrman1 was the
first to point out the change, writing:

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.940
"In Endgame, you can see Korg has moss forming
on his rocks that was not there in Ragnorok,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.620
showing how gross the lives of the 'boys'
have become."

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.200
Though some eagle-eyed viewers noticed during
the movie's theatrical run, it's easy to miss

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.670
this subtle visual signifier during the scene,
considering it's the introduction of the version

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.880
of Thor the directors called "Bro Thor."

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.980
Thor's extra pounds the result of five years
of terrible eating habits, even worse drinking

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:16.280
habits, and sitting around playing Fortnite
have been the subject of all manner of commentary

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.820
since Endgame's release.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.160
While some fans lamented the fact that the
Asgardian's weight gain, fueled by depression

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:26.670
over his failure to stop Thanos from decimating
half of all life in the universe, was played

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.180
for cheap jokes, others were positively moved
by the filmmakers' sensitive treatment of

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.960
what seemed to be PTSD.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.720
Helped along by Chris Hemsworth's performance,
Endgame accomplished what no previous Marvel

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:42.120
film had done: it brought the God of Thunder
down to Earth, showing us mere mortals that

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.140
not even he is immune from depression and
its effects.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:46.480
"No.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.860
Yes.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.520
I think I'm losing it."

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:57.120
There was a heck of a lot going on in Endgame's
entire 3-plus hour run time, so fans could

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.350
be forgiven for overlooking a few patches
of creeping foliage.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.960
But, now that we've pointed it out, you won't
be able to unsee it.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:08.200
It's an understated way to suggest that Thor
isn't the only one who has been sitting on

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.500
his butt for five years.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.190
Thankfully, we'll almost certainly get to
see more of Korg, and perhaps he will have

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.610
cleaned himself up a bit.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:19.510
Thor: Ragnarok director Taika Waititi, who
voices the lovable stack of stones, has officially

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:23.370
signed on to helm Thor: Love and Thunder,
which will make Odinson the first Avenger

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.640
to get a fourth solo outing.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.040
The movie, scheduled to hit screens November
5, 2021, will see the return of Natalie Portman

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.591
as Jane Foster, who will follow the character's
comics arc by taking up Mjolnir to become

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.480
the Mighty Thor.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.840
Where that iteration of Mjolnir will come
from, since Captain America returned the one

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.940
from 2013 back to its time, is a question
yet to be answered.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.110
We can only imagine Korg's reaction to this
development.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.040
Will he think that the Odinson has somehow
become a woman?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.380
"Sounds like you had a pretty special and
intimate relationship with this hammer and

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.140
that losing it was almost comparable to losing
a loved one."

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.540
At any rate, Korg's little hygiene problem
in Endgame illustrates the fact that this

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:05.810
massive film is probably still hiding scores
of small but significant details, and it wouldn't

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.980
surprise us if more than a few of them are
still yet to be noticed by fandom at large.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:14.120
Of course, scouring the flick for every last
hidden treasure just got a lot easier with

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:18.209
its digital release, and if physical media
is more your speed, it'll be out on Blu Ray

00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:20.160
and DVD August 13.

